WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.561
An ablation separates the two components.

00:00:02.641 --> 00:00:06.619
When old and new datasets share a similar feature
distribution,

00:00:06.699 --> 00:00:09.905
adaptive weight modification does most of the work,

00:00:09.985 --> 00:00:12.288
and removing it sharply raises error.

00:00:12.368 --> 00:00:16.347
When the datasets are recorded under very different
conditions,

00:00:16.427 --> 00:00:20.534
the regularization term becomes the key to
overcoming forgetting.

00:00:20.614 --> 00:00:22.982
Across the full four-dataset sequence,

00:00:23.062 --> 00:00:28.006
removing adaptive weight modification hurts more
than removing regularization,

00:00:28.086 --> 00:00:32.580
so it is the primary driver, with regularization a
valuable complement.
